horn), central Italy, located on a plot of land near the Via Verdi, close to the Waldensian Church and to the formerly Anglican church of St. George. It is the oldest Protestant cemetery in Italy.","wpu":"Old English Cemetery, Livorno","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/35/View_of_the_English_Burial_Ground_at_Leghorn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Diocese of Livorno","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":43.55,"lo":10.316667,"d":997,"ds":"The Diocese of Livorno (Latin: Dioecesis Liburnensis) is a Latin diocese of the Catholic Church in Tuscany. It was created in 1806. It is a suffragan of the Archdiocese of Pisa.","wpu":"Diocese of Livorno","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Duomo_Livorno.JPG/960px-Duomo_Livorno.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Santa Maria del Soccorso, Livorno","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":43.5456,"lo":10.3165,"d":1239,"ds":"Santa Maria del Soccorso (Our Lady of the Rescue) is a Neoclassical style, Roman Catholic, Marian votive church in central Livorno. The tall brick church facade is located scenically at the end of Via Magenta, and has a park surrounding it. In front is a Monument to Fallen Soldiers (Caduti) in the first World War.","wpu":"Santa Maria del Soccorso, Livorno","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Chiesa_Santa_Madonna_del_Soccorso%2C_Livorno.jpg/960px-Chiesa_Santa_Madonna_del_Soccorso%2C_Livorno.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Meloria","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":43.548017,"lo":10.219095,"d":6945,"ds":"Meloria is a rocky skerry, surrounded by a shoal, off the Tuscan coast, in the Ligurian Sea, 6.1 kilometres (3.8 mi) north-west of Livorno.","wpu":"Meloria","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Primo_bagno_della_stagione.jpg/960px-Primo_bagno_della_stagione.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Fonte di San Fele","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":43.49534,"lo":10.35039,"d":7382,"ds":"The Fonte di San Fele is a fountain in Montenero, Livorno, Italy. It is named after a religious building (Pieve di San Fele), which identity is unclear, cited in 1082 as part of the plover of Saint Paul in Ardenza. It is a very simple structure consisting in a semicircular basin set against a stone-clad backdrop and a small side drain.","wpu":"Fonte di San Fele","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Fonte_S_Fele_Livorno.JPG/960px-Fonte_S_Fele_Livorno.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sanctuary of Montenero","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":43.4927,"lo":10.3499,"d":7619,"ds":"The Shrine of Our Lady of Grace, also known as Sanctuary of Montenero, is a religious complex in Monte Nero, a village in Livorno Hills, near Livorno, central Italy reachable by a funicular. The complex, elevated to the rank of Basilica and maintained by Vallombrosian monks, is devoted to Our Lady of Grace of Montenero, patron of Tuscany. It also includes a rich gallery of votive offerings.","wpu":"Sanctuary of Montenero","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Santuario_di_montenero_01.JPG/960px-Santuario_di_montenero_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Moby Prince disaster","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":43.483333,"lo":10.266667,"d":8340,"ds":"The Moby Prince disaster was a major maritime accident resulting in 140 deaths. It occurred in the late evening of Wednesday 10 April 1991, in the harbour of Livorno, Italy. It is the worst disaster in the Italian merchant navy since World War II.","wpu":"Moby Prince disaster","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d3/Moby_Prince.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Meloria north end Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":43.59,"lo":10.211667,"d":8571,"ds":"Meloria north end Lighthouse (Italian: Faro Nord delle Secche della Meloria) is an active lighthouse located in the Ligurian Sea, 7.5 nautical miles (13.9 km; 8.6 mi) north of Meloria south end Lighthouse and 7.5 nautical miles (13.9 km; 8.6 mi) north west of Livorno, in the northern part of the Meloria shoal.","wpu":"Meloria north end Lighthouse","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/Meloria_north_lighthouse_01_%40chesi.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Pisa International Airport (IATA: PSA, ICAO: LIRP) — also named Galileo Galilei Airport — is an international airport located in Pisa, Italy. It is one of the two major airports in Tuscany, the other being Florence Airport. Pisa is ranked 10th in Italy in terms of passenger numbers.","wpu":"Pisa International Airport","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Pisa_International_Airport_Galileo_Galilei%2C_Italy.JPG/960px-Pisa_International_Airport_Galileo_Galilei%2C_Italy.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}